// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ARDUINO IDE PROTOTYPE INJECTION FIX
//  Arduino IDE inserts auto-generated function prototypes at the very
//  beginning of the merged .cpp file — before any user code including
//  #pragma and #include directives. Any type appearing in a function
//  signature (return type or parameter) must therefore be declared in a
//  SEPARATE HEADER that Arduino pulls in before prototype injection, OR
//  the type must be declared via an #include that precedes all code.
//
//  The only reliable way in a single .ino file is to put struct/enum
//  declarations BEFORE the first #include, using only primitive types.
//  Arduino's -E preprocessing pass processes all #includes so Arduino
//  types (String, std::vector) are available during prototype extraction,
//  but the struct bodies must appear textually first in the merged file.
//
//  All structs used as function parameters/return types are declared here.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
